{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837962",
      "title": "Getting User Input via Refs",
      "sourceHash": "5f15978e9c8bf9a97588715777e41e453a9968f14fa8fe0bb2660a6a77d9e157",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 5.6,
          "en": "Now extracting values with help of useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.73,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "is one way of handling user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 12.72,
          "en": "I'll now copy that login component and paste it in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.72,
          "end": 16.68,
          "en": "and just name the file state login so that we'll keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.68,
          "end": 21.45,
          "en": "that code where we use useState for tracking the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.45,
          "end": 25.95,
          "en": "in this file so that I can go back to the login JSX file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 25.95,
          "end": 29.85,
          "en": "and clear that state code from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 29.85,
          "end": 33.57,
          "en": "I'll keep handle submit but I'll clear the state code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 33.57,
          "end": 36.993,
          "en": "and the change handling functions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 42.36,
          "en": "I'll also get rid of on change and the value props here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 42.36,
          "end": 45.72,
          "en": "on those input elements because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.72,
          "end": 49.593,
          "en": "that was just one possible way of handling user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 53.88,
          "en": "Another way would be to use refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 53.88,
          "end": 56.34,
          "en": "And, of course, you also learned about this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 56.34,
          "end": 57.633,
          "en": "before in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.59,
          "end": 63.577,
          "en": "You could set up an email ref here and a password ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 65.13,
          "end": 70.13,
          "en": "So two refs like this, and then connect those ref values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 71.34,
          "end": 74.97,
          "en": "to those input fields by adding the special ref prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 74.97,
          "end": 78.93,
          "en": "which can be set on all HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 78.93,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "So which is supported by React on all elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 83.03999999999999,
          "end": 86.64,
          "en": "And you'll learn more about refs in the dedicated refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 86.64,
          "end": 88.383,
          "en": "course section, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 89.58,
          "end": 92.34,
          "en": "So here we can set ref like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 92.34,
          "end": 97.34,
          "en": "and we can set ref here to email for this email input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 98.22,
          "end": 103.14,
          "en": "So, to this first ref here, and for the password field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 103.14,
          "end": 105.90299999999999,
          "en": "we, of course, set it to password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 107.82,
          "end": 111.36,
          "en": "Now by setting the ref prop here, connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 111.36,
          "end": 114.78,
          "en": "will be established between this DOM element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 114.78,
          "end": 118.97999999999999,
          "en": "so this input element here and this ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "And you can use this connection, for example, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 123.96,
          "en": "in handle submit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 123.96,
          "end": 126.63,
          "en": "You can use it to get the entered email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 126.63,
          "end": 131.63,
          "en": "by simply accessing email.current because you always need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 136.38,
          "en": "to access the current property on your ref objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 136.38,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "because it's this current property which will hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 142.44,
          "en": "the actual connected value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 142.44,
          "end": 146.25,
          "en": "So the input object value here in case of email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 146.25,
          "end": 147.083,
          "en": "and password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 148.07999999999998,
          "end": 152.49,
          "en": "And then since the value will be this input DOM element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 152.49,
          "end": 154.92000000000002,
          "en": "object that is being stored here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 154.92000000000002,
          "end": 159.3,
          "en": "you can access a value property on that object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 159.3,
          "end": 162.27,
          "en": "because every input DOM element object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 162.27,
          "end": 164.613,
          "en": "will have such a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 165.48,
          "end": 169.53,
          "en": "And you can repeat this approach for the entered password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 173.733,
          "en": "and get that by accessing password.current.value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 174.72,
          "end": 178.71,
          "en": "And now you can also use these values and output the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 178.71,
          "end": 181.833,
          "en": "entered email and the entered password like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 183.99,
          "end": 187.74,
          "en": "And if you do this and you save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 187.74,
          "end": 192.74,
          "en": "if I again enter an email and a password and I click log in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 193.98,
          "end": 196.443,
          "en": "I get those values here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 197.52,
          "end": 200.25,
          "en": "And that's there for another way of getting hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 200.25,
          "end": 203.31,
          "en": "of those values and of course, the advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 203.31,
          "end": 204.99,
          "en": "of using this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 204.99,
          "end": 208.26,
          "en": "is that it typically requires less code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 208.26,
          "end": 210.81,
          "en": "than when using state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 210.81,
          "end": 214.44,
          "en": "After all, we did not have to add any change handling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 214.44,
          "end": 218.7,
          "en": "functions or add the on change or value props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 218.7,
          "end": 220.59,
          "en": "to the input elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 220.59,
          "end": 224.57999999999998,
          "en": "All we had to do is create those refs, connect them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 224.57999999999998,
          "end": 229.083,
          "en": "with the ref prop, and then extract the values like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 230.97,
          "end": 235.97,
          "en": "The downside of this approach is that resetting those values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 240.39,
          "en": "in a clean way is a bit harder because you are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 240.39,
          "end": 245.39,
          "en": "actually discouraged to use refs for manipulating the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 246.27,
          "end": 249.09,
          "en": "So resetting them like this would work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 249.09,
          "end": 253.53,
          "en": "but is actually not recommended or at least something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 253.53,
          "end": 255.66,
          "en": "you should use with care.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 255.66,
          "end": 260.07,
          "en": "And, of course, you'll still end up with quite a lot of refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 260.07,
          "end": 264.51,
          "en": "if you have a more complex form and you'll have to set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 264.51,
          "end": 267.99,
          "en": "and connect all those refs manually step by step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 267.99,
          "end": 270.33,
          "en": "which can become quite some work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 270.33,
          "end": 273.663,
          "en": "if you are dealing with multiple input elements.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}